  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>On this peninsula famous for its luxury villas, part of the Cros deï Pin beach, to the north, welcomes dogs on a leash — with the option of swimming, which isn't a given at the other spots in the area.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The area sits just above the Saint-Jean-Cap-Ferrat harbour — an easy landmark for finding the dog-friendly section without mistaking it for the rest of the beach.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the Sentier des Douaniers coastal path that loops around the peninsula is a great walk to pair with the swim, even though dogs aren't allowed on a leash everywhere along it — best to check locally.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Villefranche-sur-Mer and its Ange Gardien beach are a few minutes away, a good option if this one is too crowded.</p>
